{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_0","type":"agent_message","text":"I’ll verify the r11 gate and its measured limits, then build the complete corpus claim plan and measure the missing verification phases before freezing the declaration. The 69,936 ms pilot stays in the record as a pre-declaration observation."}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_1","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc 'cat collab/yang-clojure/1794731000000-engineer-d1-r11-declaration-verifier-integration.gpt-6.1-terra.findings.md'","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_1","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc 'cat collab/yang-clojure/1794731000000-engineer-d1-r11-declaration-verifier-integration.gpt-6.1-terra.findings.md'","aggregated_output":"# D1 r11 — bounded fixture-gate integration and pre-declaration pilots\n\nStatus: **partial; no complete bounds declaration, bounded corpus verification, D1 companion or verification result**. Worktree mirror; no commit. The retained r9e store under `target/d1-r9e-retained-store` stays uncommitted and its retention location/owner remains pending. The r9g sequencing resolution authorizes labeled pre-declaration pilots and requires any verification run to follow a frozen declaration.\n\n## Integrated fixture gate\n\n`test/yang/correspondence_verification.clj` composes the independent `check-fixture!` static gate, a required `:site-declarations` refusal of a mutated declaration, each lane's per-step runtime checker and the independent scoped `attributed?` query for a nonempty supplied claim set. It preserves the trace data and measured runtime information and labels its output `:not-a-d1-verification-result true`: this is not a complete D1 verifier and does not establish recipe, image derivation, instruction provenance or full corpus credit coverage. It refuses missing completed lanes and missing trace-graph sizers; measured maximum exceedances are returned as `:failed-bound` with observed value and ceiling. A post-halt graph-size bound and fixture wall-time checks at phase boundaries are supported; the latter do not interrupt a long host operation mid-phase. The runtime checker monitors logical printed trace bytes and steps between guest steps, sampled JVM used heap and lane elapsed time; it does not enforce an OS/native-memory limit and a single step can temporarily exceed limits before detection. Reaching the step budget without halting is a refusal; do not misreport the unexecuted next step as a measured exceedance.\n\nRow retrieval now accepts an explicit maximum rather than always using the 100,000-row pilot default. `bounded-tree-statistics!` checks rows, occurrence and application counts, depth and encoded application-path bytes as it walks, before invoking either lane. It does not independently cap the byte size of one row or initial row retrieval; a real driver must enforce those as well. The integrated gate has tests for real static declaration reconstruction using synthetic ASTs, simulated bounded lanes, scoped attribution, input mutation, missing lane, empty claims, a failed bound with preserved evidence, missing/oversized trace-graph measurement, tree limit refusal and fixture time failure. Passing these tests is not a corpus verification.\n\n## Guard pilot and material timing finding\n\nThe first pre-declaration guard pilot used the r10 candidate limits, replayed retained programs, re-fetched both closures and queried all symbol-valued static callees at arities 0–4; it is an exploratory query set, not the required full upstream attribution/credit set. `1794731000000-engineer-d1-r11-guard-pilot.edn` records two passes, 1/5 and 100/700 exploratory queries credited. The timed variant (`1794731000000-engineer-d1-r11-guard-pilot-timed.edn`, `target/d1-r11-guard-pilot-timed.log`) additionally sized the halted trace graph. For `:check-assume-have-discharge`, walker/semantic steps were 2,544,482 / 1,398,649, lane wall 18,679 / 7,789 ms, trace graph 311,144 bytes each, 2,345 records / 67,500 printed bytes each, and the integrated static/mutation/lanes/query gate took **59,390 ms**. The 60,000 ms candidate from r10 would have only 610 ms (~1%) headroom and is not adequate to finalize as a headroom-supported ceiling. That gate timing excludes the initial store reopen, retained input fetch and replay compilation. Candidate values were not a declared run and no bounded-verification result is claimed.\n\nA further pre-declaration two-fixture pilot `target/d1-r11-guard-pilot-complete.clj` completed with the newer tree checks and explicit graph sizer. Its outcome record is `1794731000000-engineer-d1-r11-guard-pilot-complete.edn`; the later retained-path pilot is described below. Its 180,000 ms fixture safety setting is a pilot setting, not a frozen declaration or permission to raise a declared bound.\n\n## Remaining work\n\nThe r10 candidate table remains non-binding. A complete finite measured declaration still requires comparable full guarded-fixture and phase timings (including fetch/replay and query), defensible headroom including the 59,390 ms observation, byte/memory capacity enforcement and the required true B/S provenance production/persistence/loading/query and cold/warm comparisons. The prior B/S path-index benchmark is not that full experiment. The fixture gate still needs a real corpus driver with declaration binding, supported complete claims, all static and phase ceilings and failure persistence, as well as the design §4.2 recipe/image/derivation/instruction provenance steps. There is no complete D1 record or address to cite, so no companion or verification result has been fabricated. The entire oracle suite was not run.\n\n## Retained-input fixture gate and latest pilot\n\n`verify-retained-fixture!` now joins the r9e outcome to retained input,\nsnapshot, complete row closures, evidence and exact capture profile; it\nrecompiles the captured program/options and requires the recorded root, then\npasses the reconstructed static input and caller-supplied claims into the\nbounded fixture gate. It uses the original recorded admission coordinate,\nnot a newly minted one. It checks the requested row-fetch ceiling and maps a\nfetch-limit refusal to structured `:failed-bound` evidence: `:observed` is\nthe lower bound on distinct required addresses encountered, explicitly\nlabeled `:distinct-required-addresses`; it does not claim the extra row was\nsuccessfully fetched. Fixture elapsed is checked at host phase boundaries;\nper-step checks apply only within each lane. The progress writer now attempts\nto fsync the directory after its atomic rename, best-effort on hosts that do\nnot support directory syncing.\n\nThe final two-fixture, **pre-declaration** retained-path pilot\n`1794731000000-engineer-d1-r11-retained-pilot.edn` (SHA-256\n`fce5f750ca1e46b4ee25850cf874a80d6d9e7e6ea0fd46d83787bc40fe2d3b76`)\nrecorded two passes: `:minimal-last` 3,245 ms and\n`:check-assume-have-discharge` 68,932 ms including fetch, replay and fixture\ngate but excluding opening the store. Its exploratory static-callee arities\n0–4 produced 1/5 and 100/700 credits. It is not the full upstream claim set,\nnot a D1 verifier result and not a declared bounded run. Earlier complete\npilot measured the larger fixture at 69,876 ms; both exceed the old 60,000 ms\nnon-binding combined-fixture candidate. A possible 150,000 ms candidate is\nnot a finalized ceiling; the full corpus and store-open/phase measurements\nunder this final code are still absent.\n\nThe gate refuses empty claims and incomplete fixture, tree, lane or graph-size\nbounds before running a lane. It also refuses a missing graph sizer and checks\npost-halt reachable trace graph bytes against the supplied ceiling. Failed\nbounds include the lane where relevant and preserve observed/ceiling values.\nPer-step ring, printed-byte, elapsed and sampled-heap checks, and phase-boundary\nfixture-time checks, are useful but do not form an operating-system memory\ncap or interrupt a long host phase; real-process failure supervision and full\nstatic serialized-object bounds remain unimplemented. The user-required D1\nrecord/recipe, complete upstream carrier/claim reconstruction, image and\ninstruction derivation/provenance verification and publication remain open.\nNo complete declaration, corpus bounded verification, companion or result\nexists; nothing here authorizes reliance.\n\nFinal focused correspondence tests passed **33 tests / 114 assertions**, zero failures or errors; clj-kondo on the eight correspondence support/test files reported **0 errors and 0 warnings**. `git diff --check` passed. No commit was made.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_2","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"cat target/d1-r11-retained-pilot.clj; sed -n '286,331p' collab/yang-clojure/1794670000000-architect-callsite-generalization-design.gpt-6-astra.findings.md\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_2","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"cat target/d1-r11-retained-pilot.clj; sed -n '286,331p' collab/yang-clojure/1794670000000-architect-callsite-generalization-design.gpt-6-astra.findings.md\"","aggregated_output":"(require '[yang.correspondence-verification :as verification]\n         '[yang.correspondence-measure :as measure]\n         '[yang.correspondence-batch :as batch]\n         '[yang.latte-oracle-test :as oracle]\n         '[yang.clojure :as yang]\n         '[yin.repl.store :as store]\n         '[dao.jing :as jing])\n(let [source (batch/read-progress \"collab/yang-clojure/1794720000000-engineer-d1-r9e.outcomes.edn\")\n      out \"collab/yang-clojure/1794731000000-engineer-d1-r11-retained-pilot.edn\"\n      ids [:minimal-last :check-assume-have-discharge]\n      _ (when-not (.exists (java.io.File. out))\n          (measure/initialize! out ids {:scope :r11-retained-gate-predeclaration-pilot\n                                        :pre-declaration-tagged-execution true}))\n      h (store/open {:type :file :dir \"target/d1-r9e-retained-store\"})\n      registry ((ns-resolve 'yang.latte-oracle-test 'oracle-registry) yang/kind-module)\n      rt (Runtime/getRuntime) clock #(System/nanoTime)\n      heap #(- (.totalMemory rt) (.freeMemory rt))\n      limits {:walker {:steps 4000000 :elapsed-ms 60000 :heap-bytes 6000000000\n                       :trace-records 5000 :trace-record-bytes 100 :trace-bytes 150000\n                       :trace-heap-bytes 650000}\n              :semantic {:steps 2200000 :elapsed-ms 60000 :heap-bytes 6000000000\n                         :trace-records 5000 :trace-record-bytes 100 :trace-bytes 150000\n                         :trace-heap-bytes 650000}}\n      opts {:trace-size-fn #(CorrespondenceSizeAgent/deepBytes %)\n            :fixture-limit-ms 180000\n            :tree-limits {:rows 20000 :occurrences 75000 :applications 20000\n                          :depth 750 :application-path-bytes 6000000}}]\n  (try\n    (doseq [id ids :when (= :not-run (get-in (measure/read-progress out) [:outcomes id :status]))]\n      (let [outcome (get-in source [:outcomes id])\n            evidence (jing/get h (get-in outcome [:addresses :evidence]) ::missing)\n            row (get-in evidence [:fixtures id])\n            names (into #{} (keep (fn [[_ v]] (when (symbol? (:callee v)) (:callee v)))) (:site-table row))\n            claims (vec (for [sym names arity (range 5)]\n                          {:guest-symbol sym :requested-arity arity :carriers []}))\n            result (try (assoc (verification/verify-retained-fixture! h id outcome claims limits registry clock heap opts)\n                               :pilot-limits-not-declared true\n                               :claim-scope :fixture-static-callees-arities-zero-through-four)\n                        (catch Exception e {:status :refused :stage (or (:stage (ex-data e)) :harness)\n                                            :rule (:rule (ex-data e)) :message (ex-message e)\n                                            :pilot-limits-not-declared true}))]\n        (measure/record! out id result)\n        (prn {:fixture id :status (:status result) :stage (:stage result)\n              :quantity (:quantity result) :observed (:observed result) :ceiling (:ceiling result)\n              :claims (count (:claims result)) :credited (count (filter true? (:attributed result)))\n              :fixture-ms (:fixture-elapsed-ms result)\n              :lane-ms (into {} (map (fn [[k v]] [k (:run-ms v)]) (:lanes result)))}) (flush)))\n    (finally (store/close! h))))\n(shutdown-agents)\n## 6. Measurement and declared budgets\n\nThese are measurement requirements and design cost models, **not measured performance claims**. Signed A3 requires a budget impact per frontend, and line 29 requires static/runtime separation. This read-only design has no authority to invent benchmark results. Numeric per-corpus totals remain **unknown — the implementation round's inventory decides by measuring the pinned baseline before tagged runs**.\n\n### 6.1 Counts and cost model\n\nFor each fixture/prelude/module, host, and format record:\n\n- `U`: distinct canonical rows; `O`: all occurrence-tree positions; `A`: `:application` occurrences; `D`: maximum path depth; `L`: total encoded length of application paths; separate user, helper, wrapper, prelude, macro-generated and Rule-R counts as derived diagnostic groups.\n- `P_f`: instruction count/provenance-row count for format f; report shared semantic/native mapping structures separately if used.\n- `S_static`: exact encoded bytes of C1 rows, provenance tables, retained origin records, D1 and its reconstruction inputs; distinguish fresh bytes from already retained shared content, index memory and storage/dedup savings.\n- `E`: actual callee-entry records, per-lane total bytes and maximum record size; `Q_peak`: peak retained trace records and bytes, dropped/blocked writes and drain schedule.\n- Guest instruction counts and host-side work counters; wall compile/expand/project/publish/verify/load/query time; process/heap peak and retained memory, including trace buffers, indexes and pending continuations.\n\nOccurrence counts can greatly exceed unique row counts because identical subtrees are shared; an `O(U)` annotation-size promise would be false (code-as-tuples `:393-404,636-665,947-949`). A direct marker representation costs one row per A plus encoded paths/origins: storage proportional to `A + L + coordinate bytes`; traversal work proportional to visited occurrences, not unique content. Instruction mapping adds up to `P_f` rows per claimed format with path/coordinate payload. The exact peak depends on streaming vs retaining both trees/tables and must be measured.\n\n### 6.2 Experiment separation\n\nUse the same pinned code-producing inputs and three configurations:\n\n1. **B — baseline:** existing code, trace disabled.\n2. **S — static annotation:** C1/provenance production, persistence, loading and query enabled; runtime trace disabled.\n3. **T — tagged tracing:** same S outputs plus caller propagation and body-entry recording.\n\nAlso compare the oracle's existing two-field tracing with T to isolate the extra caller-site field from the original body-entry instrumentation. Report S−B and T−S separately, and the old-trace→tagged-trace delta. If instrumentation itself changes code, keep its canonical image and compile cost separate from side-only annotation. Static C1 must change **zero canonical code bytes/addresses and zero guest instructions** for otherwise identical input; runtime tracing has no such zero-cost claim.\n\nMeasure cold and warm compile/load/query separately; use fresh publication caches for cold tests, fixed workload/repetition count and host/version, and publish distribution plus raw samples rather than an unqualified single timing. Report query indexes/build time separately from query execution. Do not call a host trace hook “zero overhead” because guest instruction count did not increase.\n\n### 6.3 Bounds published before any tagged run\n\nThe implementation preflight record must contain actual finite numbers (no “TBD”, unlimited trace, or post-run adjustment) for:\n\n| Bound | Required derivation / failure |\n|---|---|\n| Maximum input rows, occurrences, A, D and total path bytes | Derive from the pinned static corpus; reject over-bound traversal before instrumentation. Include generated/bundled prelude expansion, not only source calls. |\n| Static side bytes and retained memory | Measure S without tracing; declare maximum per artifact/module and aggregate closure. Serialization size may be computed exactly before execution. Stop/revise on exceeding the declared storage/memory bound. |\n| Maximum records E and trace capacity C | Bound accepted trace writes for the fixture, declare C in records AND bytes including worst allowed site-id/path length, and declare drain behavior. No credit from a truncated/overflowed trace. |\n| Guest instruction ceiling and added work | Bound trace instructions per event/dispatch under each executed format, plus fixed setup/drain costs. Declare a ceiling for each host/format run before T; report baseline, absolute delta and ratio. |\n| Compile/expand/publish/verify/load/query time | Declare finite absolute time limits and allowed deltas against B/S in the preflight record. Pilot B/S measurements may set these; a tagged timeout is a failed bounded run. |\n| Peak process/heap/trace/index/continuation memory | Declare finite ceilings and measurement method; if a host lacks a heap counter, use a named process-memory measure and mark comparability limits. Missing measurement is not zero usage. |\n\nFor the oracle specifically, current code uses trace capacity **1,000,000 records**, drains after halt, and allows **4,000,000 guest instructions per C lane** (`latte_oracle_test.clj:1827,1847-1854,2453-2454`). These are the inspected baseline settings, not evidence the tagged run fits. Its own note records 2,024,912 walker and 1,105,792 semantic steps for the older binding fixture at line 2454. Restate both ceilings, the new record byte bound and the occupancy argument before T. If the implementation cannot establish enough capacity under those ceilings, publish revised bounds and their justification before running tagged evidence. Never silently raise fuel to get credit, or let a full trace stream park the fixture and misclassify it as semantic failure.\n\nFor other frontends, no oracle 4M/1M setting is inherited by default. Their adoption preflight must give numeric ceilings for each required fixture/prelude/host and format. Exceeding a declared bound blocks that acceptance run; changing bounds creates a new versioned run declaration and preserves the failed run.\n\n### 6.4 Budget impact allocated per frontend\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_3","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"cat test/yang/correspondence_verification.clj; sed -n '1435,1495p' test/yang/latte_oracle_test.clj; sed -n '1860,1905p' test/yang/latte_oracle_test.clj\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_3","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"cat test/yang/correspondence_verification.clj; sed -n '1435,1495p' test/yang/latte_oracle_test.clj; sed -n '1860,1905p' test/yang/latte_oracle_test.clj\"","aggregated_output":"(ns yang.correspondence-verification\n  \"A bounded fixture attribution gate. This is not the complete D1 verifier.\"\n  (:require [dao.jing :as jing]\n            [yang.clojure :as yang]\n            [yang.correspondence-text :as text]\n            [yang.correspondence-lane :as lane]\n            [yang.correspondence-measure :as measure]\n            [yang.correspondence-verifier :as verifier]\n            [yin.vm :as vm]))\n\n(defn- check-configuration! [lane-limits {:keys [trace-size-fn fixture-limit-ms tree-limits]}]\n  (when-not (and (nat-int? fixture-limit-ms)\n                 (= #{:walker :semantic} (set (keys lane-limits)))\n                 (= #{:rows :occurrences :applications :depth :application-path-bytes}\n                    (set (keys tree-limits)))\n                 (every? (fn [[_ v]] (nat-int? v)) tree-limits)\n                 (every? (fn [[_ v]]\n                           (and (= #{:steps :elapsed-ms :heap-bytes :trace-records\n                                     :trace-record-bytes :trace-bytes :trace-heap-bytes}\n                                   (set (keys v)))\n                                (every? (fn [[_ x]] (nat-int? x)) v))) lane-limits))\n    (throw (ex-info \"Incomplete fixture bounds\" {:stage :bound-declaration})))\n  (when-not (ifn? trace-size-fn)\n    (throw (ex-info \"Trace heap sizer missing\" {:stage :trace-memory}))))\n\n(defn verify-fixture!\n  \"Independently check static fixture data, require a mutated declaration\n   refusal, run both bounded lanes and execute each scoped attribution query.\n   Exceptions other than a measured bound exceedance propagate. A pass here\n   does not verify the D1 recipe, image derivations or provenance closure.\"\n  [input claims lane-limits modules clock heap & [{:keys [trace-size-fn fixture-limit-ms tree-limits started] :as options}]]\n  (let [started (or started (clock))\n        elapsed (fn [t] (quot (+ (- (clock) t) 999999) 1000000))\n        check-fixture-time! (fn []\n                              (when (some? fixture-limit-ms)\n                                (measure/check-bounds! {:fixture-ms fixture-limit-ms}\n                                                       {:fixture-ms (elapsed started)})))]\n   (try\n    (when-not (and (vector? claims) (seq claims)\n                   (every? (fn [claim] (and (map? claim) (symbol? (:guest-symbol claim))\n                                            (some? (:requested-arity claim))\n                                            (sequential? (:carriers claim)))) claims))\n      (throw (ex-info \"Missing or malformed attribution claims\" {:stage :claims})))\n    (check-configuration! lane-limits options)\n    (when tree-limits\n      (doseq [k [:before :stamped]]\n        (measure/bounded-tree-statistics! (vm/ast->semantic-bytecode (get input k)) tree-limits)))\n    (verifier/check-fixture! input)\n    (check-fixture-time!)\n    (let [site (first (keys (:site-table input)))\n          _ (when-not site (throw (ex-info \"No declaration to mutate\" {:stage :mutation})))\n          changed (assoc-in input [:site-table site :arg-shapes] [:r11-forged])\n          mutation (try (verifier/check-fixture! changed) nil\n                        (catch clojure.lang.ExceptionInfo e (:stage (ex-data e))))\n          _ (when-not (= :site-declarations mutation)\n              (throw (ex-info \"Mutated declaration was not refused\" {:stage :mutation})))\n          _ (check-fixture-time!)\n          root (:root (vm/ast->semantic-bytecode (:before input)))\n          lanes (into {}\n                      (for [[backend lane-id] [[:walker :c-walker] [:semantic :c-semantic]]]\n                        (try\n                         (let [limits (get lane-limits backend)\n                              runtime-limits (dissoc limits :trace-heap-bytes)\n                              _ (when (and (contains? limits :trace-heap-bytes) (not (ifn? trace-size-fn)))\n                                  (throw (ex-info \"Trace heap sizer missing\" {:stage :trace-memory})))\n                              lane-start (clock)\n                              checker (measure/runtime-checker runtime-limits lane-start clock heap)\n                              {:keys [machine steps]} (lane/run-measured!\n                                                        (:stamped input) modules backend\n                                                        (:steps limits) {:check! checker})\n                              run-ms (elapsed lane-start)\n                              _ (checker steps machine)\n                              ref (get-in machine [:store 'gate-execution-trace])\n                              h (get-in machine [:resources (:id ref)])\n                              _ (when-not (and (vm/halted? machine) h)\n                                  (throw (ex-info \"Lane did not halt with trace\"\n                                                  {:stage :lane-completion :lane backend})))\n                              graph-bytes (when (contains? limits :trace-heap-bytes)\n                                            (lane/trace-reachable-heap! h trace-size-fn))\n                              _ (when (some? graph-bytes)\n                                  (measure/check-bounds! {:trace-heap-bytes (:trace-heap-bytes limits)}\n                                                         {:trace-heap-bytes graph-bytes}))\n                              trace (lane/read-trace! h)\n                              _ (check-fixture-time!)]\n                          [lane-id (cond-> {:status :completed :complete? true\n                                    :executed-calls (:records trace)\n                                    :steps steps :run-ms run-ms :record-count (:record-count trace)\n                                    :serialized-bytes (:serialized-bytes trace)\n                                    :max-record-bytes (:max-record-bytes trace)}\n                                     (some? graph-bytes) (assoc :trace-heap-bytes graph-bytes))])\n                         (catch clojure.lang.ExceptionInfo e\n                           (throw (ex-info (ex-message e) (assoc (ex-data e) :lane backend) e))))))\n          attributed (mapv #(verifier/attributed?\n                              (merge % {:site-table (:site-table input)\n                                        :bindings (:bindings input) :origin (:origin input)\n                                        :root root :lanes lanes})) claims)\n          _ (check-fixture-time!)]\n      {:status :pass :fixture (:fixture input) :mutation-refusal mutation\n       :attributed attributed :claims claims :lanes lanes :elapsed-ms (elapsed started)\n       :not-a-d1-verification-result true})\n    (catch clojure.lang.ExceptionInfo e\n      (if (= :bound-exceeded (:stage (ex-data e)))\n        (merge {:status :failed-bound :fixture (:fixture input)\n                :not-a-d1-verification-result true}\n               (select-keys (ex-data e) [:stage :quantity :observed :ceiling :lane]))\n        (throw e))))))\n\n\n(defn verify-retained-fixture!\n  \"Fetch, replay and check one recorded admission before the bounded fixture\n   gate. A pass is only this gate, not a D1 verification or recipe claim.\"\n  [handle fixture outcome claims lane-limits modules clock heap options]\n  (check-configuration! lane-limits options)\n  (let [started (clock)\n        elapsed (fn [] (quot (+ (- (clock) started) 999999) 1000000))\n        check-time! (fn [] (measure/check-bounds!\n                             {:fixture-ms (:fixture-limit-ms options)}\n                             {:fixture-ms (elapsed)}))]\n    (try\n      (let [addresses (:addresses outcome)\n            {:keys [before stamped]} (measure/check-retained-trees!\n                                       handle fixture outcome\n                                       {:max-rows (get-in options [:tree-limits :rows])})\n            _ (check-time!)\n            missing ::missing\n            capture (jing/get handle (:input addresses) missing)\n            snapshot (jing/get handle (:snapshot addresses) missing)\n            evidence (jing/get handle (:evidence addresses) missing)\n            profile (jing/get handle (:profile addresses) missing)\n            _ (when-not (= text/profile profile)\n                (throw (ex-info \"Unknown or incompatible capture profile\" {:stage :profile})))\n            row (get-in evidence [:fixtures fixture])\n            _ (when-not (and (= 1 (:version evidence)) (map? row))\n                (throw (ex-info \"Missing or unsupported evidence\" {:stage :evidence})))\n            _ (check-time!)\n            program (text/read-one! fixture (:program-edn capture))\n            compiler-options (text/read-one! fixture (:options-edn capture))\n            _ (verifier/check-replay-root!\n                fixture (yang/compile-program program true compiler-options) (:root snapshot))\n            _ (check-time!)\n            input (assoc snapshot\n                         :before (vm/semantic-bytecode->ast before)\n                         :stamped (vm/semantic-bytecode->ast stamped)\n                         :forms (text/read-one! fixture (:forms-edn capture))\n                         :call (text/read-one! fixture (:call-edn capture))\n                         :source-hash (:canonical-source-hash row)\n                         :site-table (:site-table row))\n            result (verify-fixture! input claims lane-limits modules clock heap\n                                    (assoc options :started started))]\n        (if (= :failed-bound (:status result))\n          result\n          (do (check-time!)\n              (assoc result :admission-origin (:admission-origin outcome)\n                            :fixture-elapsed-ms (elapsed)))))\n      (catch clojure.lang.ExceptionInfo e\n        (if (= :bound-exceeded (:stage (ex-data e)))\n          (merge {:status :failed-bound :fixture fixture :not-a-d1-verification-result true}\n                 (select-keys (ex-data e)\n                              [:stage :quantity :observed :ceiling :lane :tree :observed-kind]))\n          (throw e))))))\n        (is (agrees? a c) \"A uses updated Vars; B/C use the returned definition environment\")))))\n\n\n;; =============================================================================\n;; Slice 9: a fail-closed kernel gate. Historical slice tests are not the gate.\n;; =============================================================================\n\n(def ^:private kernel-gate-corpus\n  (edn/read-string (slurp (io/resource \"yang/latte_oracle/kernel_gate.edn\"))))\n\n\n(def ^:private kernel-fixture-closure\n  (edn/read-string (slurp (io/resource \"yang/latte_oracle/fixture_closure.edn\"))))\n\n\n(defn- kernel-symbol\n  [{:keys [ns name]}]\n  (symbol (str/replace (str ns) \"_\" \"-\") (str name)))\n\n\n(defn- kernel-guest-name\n  [s]\n  (symbol (str \"gate-\" (last (str/split (namespace s) #\"\\.\")) \"-\" (name s))))\n\n\n(defn- kernel-arities\n  [form]\n  (when (#{'defn 'defn-} (first form))\n    (let [header (drop-while #(not (or (vector? %) (seq? %))) (nnext form))\n          params (if (vector? (first header)) [(first header)] (map first header))]\n      (mapv (fn [p] (if (some #{'&} p) [:variadic (.indexOf p '&)] (count p))) params))))\n\n\n(def ^:private kernel-entries\n  (mapv (fn [entry]\n          (let [s (kernel-symbol entry)]\n            (upstream-fn s) ; load the real aliases and refers before resolving source\n            (assoc entry :symbol s :arities (kernel-arities (get top-forms [(:ns entry) (:name entry)])))))\n        manifest))\n\n\n(defn- kernel-resolve\n  [ns-sym s]\n  (when (symbol? s)\n    (let [n (the-ns (symbol (str/replace (str ns-sym) \"_\" \"-\")))\n          v (ns-resolve n s)]\n      (when (and (var? v) (str/starts-with? (str (:ns (meta v))) \"latte-kernel.\"))\n        (symbol (str (:ns (meta v))) (str (:name (meta v))))))))\n\n\n(defn- kernel-rewrite\n  \"Resolve library names against their actual upstream namespace, respecting\n   lexical binders and quote. No blanket alias stripping or data rewriting.\"\n  [ns-sym form]\n  (letfn [(bindings [pattern] (set (filter symbol? (tree-seq coll? seq pattern))))\n          (forms [xs bound] (map #(step % bound) xs))\n          (arity\n            [xs bound]\n            (let [[params & body] xs\n                  body (forms body (into bound (bindings params)))\n                  body (if (and (= ns-sym 'latte_kernel.syntax) (= 'free-vars (second form))\n          (and (symbol? s) (nil? (namespace s))\n               (not (contains? bound s))\n               (contains? kernel-ambient-bindings (kernel-resolve ns-sym s))))\n        (tree-seq coll? seq form)))\n\n\n(defn- kernel-clauses\n  \"The `[params body…]` clauses of one upstream top-level defn.\"\n  [ns-sym name]\n  (let [form (get top-forms [ns-sym name])\n        header (drop-while #(not (or (vector? %) (seq? %))) (nnext form))]\n    (if (vector? (first header)) [header] header)))\n\n\n(defn- kernel-program-clauses\n  \"The `[params body…]` clauses of `fname` among the forms the C program\n   assembles (the checked-in context layer, the guest sources, the\n   branch-local refusals), or nil when the name is not carried.\"\n  [fname]\n  (some (fn [form]\n          (when (= fname (second form))\n            (let [header (drop-while #(not (or (vector? %) (seq? %))) (nnext form))]\n              (if (vector? (first header)) [header] header))))\n        (concat context-forms (vals kernel-sources) kernel-declaration-refusals)))\n\n\n(def ^:private kernel-ambient-correspondence\n  \"The mechanically derived attribution paths (R6/R7), keyed\n   `[upstream-symbol arity]` → #{[carrier guest-arity kind]}: for each\n   admitted upstream function and arity, the guest/context callable and\n   guest arity that carry the adapted form. Three shapes are derived\n   from the pinned upstream forms and the checked-in context layer, all\n   anchored to the context layer's own convention (context.edn's header:\n   a context occupies the def-env argument throughout the adapted\n   kernel):\n   - :ambient-delegation — an upstream clause whose body is a single\n     self-delegation through the module-level ambient state (R3's\n     disjointness pair: `registered-definition?` /1) maps to the carrier\n     the adapter's mirrored stub delegates to; the credit query requires\n     such a site's compiled context argument to be the adapter-supplied\n     ambient literal.\n   - :context-shift — a carrier clause `[kernel …]`. When the upstream\n     clause at the SAME arity carries the env at its head (the pinned\n     upstream names that parameter `def-env`/`env`), the kernel replaced\n     the parameter (register-definition /2 and /3, local-definitions /1,\n     elab-opacity /3, fetch-definition, qualify-def, …); otherwise the\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
